Q: Extract Matrix of Values from Matrix using Matrix of Row Numbers A: <p>First of all, my answer does <em><strong>NOT</strong></em> give an efficient solution (I strongly recommend the method by <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79922915/extract-matrix-of-values-from-matrix-using-matrix-of-row-numbers#comment141033684_79922926">Rui Barradas</a> ).</p>
<p>But I guess the following approach might fit your expected logic</p>
<pre><code>apply(val_rows, 2, \(k) vals[k,val_col])
</code></pre>
<p>which gives</p>
<pre><code>     [,1]  [,2]  [,3] 
[1,] &quot;3x2&quot; &quot;4x2&quot; &quot;3x2&quot;
[2,] &quot;1x2&quot; &quot;3x2&quot; &quot;5x2&quot;
[3,] &quot;3x2&quot; &quot;4x2&quot; &quot;2x2&quot;
[4,] &quot;1x2&quot; &quot;5x2&quot; &quot;5x2&quot;
</code></pre>
